</div>
<a href="/static/downloads/evaluation/od11_aen6_crosslingual_ranked.csv.gz" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="px-3 py-1 bg-red-700 text-white rounded hover:bg-red-800 text-xs self-start sm:self-auto whitespace-nowrap">CSV.GZ</a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<h4 class="font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2">Recall Summary</h4>
<div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2 p-2 bg-gray-50 rounded">
<div>
<span class="font-medium">All Benchmarks — Recall Summary</span>
<span class="text-gray-500 ml-2">(aggregated results)</span>
</div>
<a href="/static/downloads/evaluation/recall_summary.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="px-3 py-1 bg-red-700 text-white rounded hover:bg-red-800 text-xs self-start sm:self-auto whitespace-nowrap">CSV</a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-200">
<p class="text-xs text-gray-500">
<strong>Columns:</strong> rank, source_ref, target_ref, source_text, target_text, fused_score, channels, channel_count, matched_words, is_gold, gold_index. Cross-lingual CSVs include cosine, dict_count, dict_words, phonetic_count. Compressed with gzip.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6" id="run-your-own">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Run your own Tesserae</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">A bundle is one archive that holds everything the search engine needs, namely the texts, the lemma caches, the search indexes, the word-pair tables, the aligned translations that are public domain or openly licensed, and the commentaries whose license allows it. With the code from GitHub and the recipe below, it runs on a machine of your own. A bundle is offered for non-commercial use, because two lemma tables and some commentaries carry non-commercial licenses; every source and its attribution line is listed in the license file inside the archive.</p>
<div class="space-y-3 mb-4">
<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2 p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded">
<div>
<span class="font-medium">Core bundle, 20 October 2026</span>
<span class="text-sm text-gray-500 ml-2">(3.1 GB compressed, about 17 GB unpacked)</span>
<p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Built from the production data at code version <span class="font-mono">9085292f</span>. SHA-256 <span class="font-mono break-all">0c953d8e2be07fd68e39a783e2c0f744990a0f45388da7ff269da396f20ebf2f</span>
</p>
</div>
<a href="/static/downloads/bundle/tesserae-public-core-20261020.tar.zst" class="px-4 py-2 bg-red-700 text-white rounded hover:bg-red-800 text-sm text-center whitespace-nowrap">Download bundle</a>
</div>
<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm">
<a href="/static/downloads/bundle/tesserae-public-core-20261020.tar.zst.sha256" class="text-red-700 hover:underline">Checksum</a>
<a href="/static/downloads/bundle/MANIFEST-core-20261020.tsv" class="text-red-700 hover:underline">Manifest (every file, size and checksum)</a>
<a href="/static/downloads/bundle/LICENSES-core-20261020.md" class="text-red-700 hover:underline">License file</a>
<a href="https://github.com/tesserae/tesserae-v6/blob/main/docs/RUN_YOUR_OWN.md" class="text-red-700 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The recipe, step by step</a>
</div>
</div>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-3">The 14 October core bundle was withdrawn on 19 October because it contained the Sahidica New Testament, whose license allows academic use only and no redistribution. This bundle, built on the night of 19 to 20 October, leaves those texts out, and so do the Coptic word index, word counts and translation list inside it. Its Coptic bigram table carries the letter spelling corrected on 19 October.</p>
<p class="text-xs text-gray-500">A full bundle, which adds the passage windows and their vectors for Similar Passages and Theme Search, is not published yet. Ask through Suggest a change in the footer if you need it.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Developer Data Files</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">These files are the other way to install a working copy, apart from the core bundle above. Each is a .tar.gz archive. Unpack it with <span class="font-mono">tar -xzf</span> into the path given on the folder page, and check it against <a href="https://tesserae.caset.buffalo.edu/tesserae-data/SHA256SUMS.txt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-600 hover:underline">SHA256SUMS.txt</a> (the checksums there are those of the archives).</p>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">To run Tesserae V6 locally, you need the Git repository plus pre-built search indexes (too large for GitHub). The repository holds the corpus texts, the lemma tables and the code. The pre-computed embeddings left the repository on 19 October 2026 and are offered as ZIP files above and in the passage window archives below. The search indexes add about 8 GB packed.</p>
<div class="bg-gray-50 rounded p-4 mb-4 overflow-x-auto">
<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-gray-700 mb-1">
<span class="text-gray-500"># 1. Clone the repository:</span>
</p>
<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-gray-800 mb-3 whitespace-nowrap">git clone https://github.com/tesserae/tesserae-v6.git</p>
<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-gray-700 mb-1">
<span class="text-gray-500"># 2. Download the search indexes (about 8 GB packed):</span>
</p>
<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-gray-800 mb-3">python scripts/download_data.py</p>
<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-gray-700 mb-1">
<span class="text-gray-500"># 3. Check that all files are present:</span>
</p>
<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-gray-800">python scripts/download_data.py --check</p>
</div>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">The download script fetches all required files automatically. You can also download individual files manually using the links below.</p>
<div class="space-y-3">
<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2 p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded">
