</div>
</div>
<p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-4">The window-text archive was withdrawn on 19 October 2026 because it held Sahidica New Testament windows, and it is offered again without them. Every archive in this list carries a LICENSE.txt and a README.txt. The Latin lemma tables, the Corpus Nummorum coins and the window texts are for non-commercial use only. The passage window archives are cut by language because the languages differ in license. The download script reads DATA_MANIFEST.json and skips files already present. See the <a href="https://github.com/tesserae/tesserae-v6/blob/main/docs/DATA_FILES_REFERENCE.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-600 hover:underline">Data Files Reference</a> for full documentation, and the <a href="https://tesserae.caset.buffalo.edu/tesserae-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-600 hover:underline">data folder</a> for the license of each archive.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow p-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">For developers</h3>
<ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5">
<li>
<a href="https://tesserae.caset.buffalo.edu/tesserae-data/tesserae-openapi.yaml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-600 hover:underline">tesserae-openapi.yaml</a> describes the web API.</li>
<li>
<a href="https://tesserae.caset.buffalo.edu/tesserae-data/tesserae_mcp.py" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-600 hover:underline">tesserae_mcp.py</a> is the local connector for AI assistants.</li>
<li>
<a href="https://tesserae.caset.buffalo.edu/tesserae-data/ai-guide.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-600 hover:underline">ai-guide.html</a> is a guide to paste into an AI assistant.</li>
<li>
<a href="https://tesserae.caset.buffalo.edu/tesserae-data/tesserae-api-privacy.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red-600 hover:underline">tesserae-api-privacy.html</a> is the privacy note for the API.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-4">
<h4 class="font-medium text-amber-900 mb-2">License Information</h4>
<p class="text-sm text-amber-800 mb-2">The texts come from open digital editions, named work by work on the Sources page with the license each carries. Most are public domain or Creative Commons Attribution (Perseus, CSEL, Corpus Corporum, Musisque Deoque and others). The Hebrew Bible text is CC BY-SA 4.0 (Miqra according to the Masorah, via Sefaria). Translations are public domain or, where marked, free for non-commercial reproduction with attribution.</p>
<p class="text-sm text-amber-800">Derived data carries its sources' terms, stated in license files inside the download: the Hebrew morphology tables (ETCBC/BHSA, CC BY-NC 4.0), the Koine Greek lemma table (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), the classical Greek lemma table (GLAUx, CC BY-SA 4.0) and the metrical scansion data (MQDQ/Pede Certo, CC BY-NC-ND 4.0). Everything else Tesserae produces, the indexes, descriptions and embeddings, is released for research and educational use.</p>
</div>
</div>
</main>
<footer class="bg-gray-100 border-t mt-8 py-4">
<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center text-sm text-gray-500">
<p>Tesserae V6</p>
</div>
</footer>
</div>"
`;

